#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0333 expect=noViolation domain=falb
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a Findings About dataset name begins with "FA", is longer than two characters, and the characters following "FA" do not match the two-character code of a domain present in the study.
#note "The lowercase Findings About split falb has suffix lb, which upper() folds to LB, the DOMAIN of LBCH. Without upper() the case-insensitive regex would let falb through and lb would not be in [FA, LB, DM]: a false violation."
dataset falb label="Findings About split, lowercase member name"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | FA | 01-701-1015
---

dataset LBCH label="Laboratory Test Results - Chemistry"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015
---
